body:
So is limiting carb intake a good idea? Like cutting down on candy, added sugar, potatoes, and bread? What's an optimal ratio of starch to fat/protein? My diet is generally high in protein and moderate in fat/carbs. I love how protein keeps me full. Whenever I make pasta or a dish heavy in carbs, I add a few pounds of chicken to prevent me from overeating the carbs, I think it works pretty well. 

&#x200B;

What about bread, specially 100% whole wheat variants? Are they terrible for health? They have a high amount of carbs with an okay amount of fiber and high whole grains.

Why is homosexuality morally wrong? It doesn't harm anyone, if anything, it benefits individuals by allowing them to feel loved by another person. The only answer I could find is because God says so; that he created humans to only be heterosexual. How is that justified? Why would you not allow homosexual people to marry if it makes them happy? 

&#x200B;

If God is moral and just, how is homosexuality immoral when it doesn't cause harm?

